; Consumer spec for the two deferred-`try_from`-SOURCE cells the named-reference fixture cannot
; hold: `map_u64_to_idx_foo` is deliberately NOT declared here, so the loose `MapU64ToIdxFoo` has no
; local owner and stays a defer candidate.
;
; (1) MAP-side deferred source. The rule ident differs from the restricted structural name
;     (`NbFooMap` vs `NonEmptyMapU64ToIdxFoo`), so the restricted class is the consumer's own and is
;     minted locally — while its `try_from` source is the LOOSE `MapU64ToIdxFoo`, which the dep's
;     index lists, so the source mint DEFERS and the conversion resolves against the dep's class.
;     The `try_from(&MapU64ToIdxFoo)` reference is conversion-internal (invisible to the field
;     walk), so its `use` can come ONLY from the emission-scope routing.
nb_foo_map = { + uint => idx_foo }

; (2) The SOLE-OWNER-SCREENED variant of the same seam. `text_table` is the sole table rule of the
;     `{* uint => text}` shape, so the loose builder is ITS class exposed as a `pub type
;     MapU64ToText = TextTable;` alias — never a deferred class, even though the dep's index also
;     lists MapU64ToText. `nb_text_table`'s `try_from` source must therefore be the LOCAL alias with
;     no dep import: the screen in `register_deferred_non_empty_map_source` is what keeps it so.
text_table = { * uint => tstr }

nb_text_table = { + uint => tstr }

; (3) REJECT set over dep-owned elements, under a rule ident that is NOT the structural name. The
;     reject emitter consults the same defer seam as every other wrapper family, and its ident
;     screen is what decides this cell: the structural name of `[* idx_foo]` under reject is
;     `IdxFooOrderedSet`, so `RejectFoos` is the consumer's OWN class — minted locally and recorded
;     in this crate's own collection index — while its loose `try_from` source IS the dep-indexed
;     `IdxFooList`, which defers. No other rule here spells a loose `[* idx_foo]`, so the source's
;     `use` can come ONLY from the reject rule's own emission-scope routing.
reject_foos = [* idx_foo] ; @duplicates reject

; (4) Exact static list over the same dependency-owned element. Its exact class is NOT in the dep
; index, so it remains local in this NON-ROOT scope; however its `try_from(&IdxFooList)` source IS
; indexed and must import from the dep collections module here. This distinguishes a local static
; carrier from a wholly deferred wrapper and pins the Vec-to-array handover's source routing. The
; named rule and its reference live in `sub.cddl`, precisely to make that import scope observable.

holder = [a: nb_foo_map, b: text_table, c: nb_text_table, d: reject_foos]
